# The M6 playthrough: a new party from New Phlan to Tyranthraxus (PlayBot, --play=).
# Chat 10: the Clue Book's area order and commissions, its rest rules, readying the best gear
# (ai-business-ideas research/pool-of-radiance-strategy.md, sections 4, 8, 10 and 11).
# travel / explore use the lab's area graph (--exits=, from tools/sweep.gd's EXIT lines).
# Squares come from the area maps (tools/lab/plan.py, evmap.py) and the original's text.

# Where to rest (the Clue Book's table, section 8). Unlisted areas camp; an interrupted camp
# still sends the party to the inn when there is a way back.
rest 3:0 inn
# Kuto's Well: nowhere until Norris is beaten (camp in the catacombs after).
rest 8:29 inn 4A24 255
# Podol Plaza: the inn until the block is quiet (0x4AE7 = 254 after nine patrols won).
rest 1:18 inn 4AE7 254
# The Textile House: not until the ogre leader and ten random fights are beaten.
rest 4:2 inn
# The Wealthy Area and the Temple of Bane: not until both blocks are cleared.
rest 1:24 inn
# Kovel Mansion: not while thieves are about.
rest 3:14 inn
# Valhingen Graveyard: not until cleared.
rest 4:10 inn
# The level the game expects of a party in each area (research/pool-of-radiance-strategy.md,
# section 4: Claude's estimates from the guides, the low end of each range). M6: a member more
# than one level below it trains, or gets the level by shortcut (logged).
level 2:20 1
level 4:21 2
level 8:29 3
level 2:15 3
level 1:18 3
level 4:2 4
level 1:24 5
level 3:14 5
level 7:17 5
level 8:27 5
level 4:10 6
level 2:9 7
level 5:3 7
level 5:4 7
level 5:5 7
level 5:6 7
level 5:7 7
# Encounters the Clue Book settles by talking: Ferran Martinez in Sokal Keep (a spectre that
# drains two levels a hit) gives his story and the word for the library.
parley 4:21 A PALE FORM RISES
# People the Clue Book says not to take along: the library's madman (trouble in town).
answer 2:15 QUITE MAD|NO
answer 2:15 DO YOU INSIST HE COME|NO
# Podol Plaza's tavern (MIX WITH MONSTERS, DRINK HEAVILY, ATTACK, LEAVE): leave.
answer 1:18 DRINK HEAVILY|LEAVE
# Cadorna's box: take it unopened (opening it loses the reward and makes him an enemy), and
# turn down the thieves' offer to copy the seal.
answer 4:2 SEAL OF THE FAMILY OF CADORNA|TAKE IT UNOPENED
answer 4:2 DUPLICATE THE SEAL|NO
# Skullcrusher, chained in the Textile House: free him with Grishnak's brass key, talk, take him on.
answer 4:2 WHAT DO YOU DO WITH THE MAN|FREE
answer 4:2 HOW WILL YOU FREE HIM|UNLOCK
answer 4:2 THERE IS A FREE MAN HERE|PARLAY
answer 4:2 ADD HIM TO YOUR PARTY|YES

# The band outside the walls (7:26) opens the city's other quarters from menus (probed in
# our engine from the band's step script, chat 10): the eastern edge 13,27, the north edge
# 12,26, the western edge 11,28.
gate 7:26 13,27 1:24 SOUTH
gate 7:26 13,27 3:14 NORTH
gate 7:26 13,27 3:0 BOAT
gate 7:26 12,26 4:10 GRAVEYARD
gate 7:26 11,28 1:18 NORTH
gate 7:26 11,28 4:2 SOUTH
# The Temple of Bane's quarter leaves by a table the area graph can't read: its east edge,
# where the band's eastern gate brings the party in, goes back out to the band.
exit 1:24 15,4 E 7:26
# The wilderness bands join at their edges (the band's on-move script: x 15 going east from
# 7:26 is 8:27, x 2 going west is 6:25; and back). The bands' sites, probed from their scripts:
# the nomad camp 7:26 12,11 (ENTER), the boats home 7:26 7,29 and 8:27 9,29, the kobolds'
# caves 8:27 6,15 and 3,18.
exit 7:26 15,12 E 8:27
exit 7:26 15,16 E 8:27
exit 7:26 15,20 E 8:27
exit 8:27 2,12 W 7:26
exit 8:27 2,16 W 7:26
exit 8:27 2,20 W 7:26
gate 7:26 12,11 7:17 ENTER
gate 7:26 7,29 3:0 TAKE BOAT
gate 8:27 9,29 3:0 YES
# The nomads (7:17): help them against the kobolds (the Clue Book: more experience and treasure
# than fighting them). Talk at the camp, follow the guard, stay and fight, finish the kobolds.
parley 7:17 THE NOMADS WAIT FOR YOU
answer 7:17 YOU TRIP ON A WIRE|ADVANCE CAUTIOUSLY
answer 7:17 FOLLOW THE GUARD|FOLLOW THE GUARD
answer 7:17 WHAT IS YOUR DECISION|STAY AND FIGHT
answer 7:17 WHAT SAY WE FINISH THIS TOGETHER|DESTROY THE KOBOLDS
# Merchants met in the wilderness are travellers, not enemies: talk to them.
parley 7:26 YOU SPOT A GROUP OF MERCHANTS
parley 8:27 YOU SPOT A GROUP OF MERCHANTS
parley 6:25 YOU SPOT A GROUP OF MERCHANTS
# Passing an edge on the way elsewhere: LEAVE (the gate's own choice comes first).
answer 7:26 EDGE OF THE CITY|LEAVE

